890
00:58:59,325 --> 00:59:01,659
What's--

891
00:59:01,724 --> 00:59:04,407
What's your thoughts on-- on--

892
00:59:04,477 --> 00:59:06,418
on how to handle this ?

893
00:59:06,492 --> 00:59:08,348
What's yours ?

894
00:59:11,292 --> 00:59:15,034
Well, I'm of the opinion
that if Marsellus lived his whole life,

895
00:59:15,099 --> 00:59:18,934
he doesn't need to know
nothing about this incident.

896
00:59:19,062 --> 00:59:21,746
If Marsellus knew
about this incident,

897
00:59:21,814 --> 00:59:23,788
I'd be in as much trouble as you.

898
00:59:23,862 --> 00:59:26,250
I seriously doubt that.

899
00:59:26,325 --> 00:59:29,141
I can keep a secret if you can.

900
00:59:31,095 --> 00:59:32,950
Shake on it ?

901
00:59:37,941 --> 00:59:40,145
Mum's the word ?

902
00:59:40,213 --> 00:59:42,068
Cool.

903
00:59:42,134 --> 00:59:46,290
Now, if you'll excuse me, I'm going
to go home and have a heart attack.

904
00:59:48,917 --> 00:59:50,771
Vincent.

905
00:59:52,566 --> 00:59:55,468
Do you wanna hear
my Fox Force Five joke ?

906
00:59:56,502 --> 00:59:58,356
Sure.

907
00:59:58,421 --> 01:00:01,324
Except I think I'm still
a little too petrified to laugh.

908
01:00:01,398 --> 01:00:04,211
No, you won't laugh
'cause it's not funny.

909
01:00:04,277 --> 01:00:07,473
But if you still wanna hear it,
I'll tell it.

910
01:00:07,540 --> 01:00:09,646
- I can't wait.
- Okay.

911
01:00:09,717 --> 01:00:12,466
Three tomatoes
are walkin' down the street.

912
01:00:12,533 --> 01:00:14,866
Papa Tomato, Mama Tomato
and Baby Tomato.

913
01:00:14,932 --> 01:00:18,926
Baby Tomato starts lagging behind,
and Papa Tomato gets really angry.

914
01:00:18,996 --> 01:00:21,810
Goes back and squishes him
and says,

915
01:00:21,875 --> 01:00:23,883
"Ketchup."

916
01:00:23,955 --> 01:00:26,542
[ Weak Chuckle ]

917
01:00:26,612 --> 01:00:28,467
Ketchup.

918
01:00:32,436 --> 01:00:34,475
See you around.

919
01:00:51,858 --> 01:00:54,609
[ Dog Barking ]

920
01:00:54,675 --> 01:00:58,220
Oh, that Paddlefoot.
He funny, silly dog.

921
01:00:58,291 --> 01:01:01,107
He think totem pole alive !

922
01:01:01,172 --> 01:01:03,789
[ Giggling ]
He arctic tenderfoot !

923
01:01:03,859 --> 01:01:07,371
[ Laughing ]
That totem pole been here forever !

924
01:01:07,443 --> 01:01:09,298
- [ Woman ] Butch ?
- [ Paddlefoot Barking ]

925
01:01:09,364 --> 01:01:12,112
[ Man On Television ]
One more thing, and we'll start for--

926
01:01:12,178 --> 01:01:14,993
- Butch, stop watching TV for a second.
- Yeah ?

927
01:01:15,058 --> 01:01:18,539
- You've got a special visitor.
- [ TV ] Stand up. Stand up.

928
01:01:21,203 --> 01:01:25,937
Now, do you remember when I told you
your daddy died in a P.O.W. camp ?

929
01:01:26,002 --> 01:01:29,581
Well, this here is Captain Koons.

930
01:01:29,651 --> 01:01:32,464
He was in the P.O.W. camp
with Daddy.

931
01:01:37,586 --> 01:01:39,440
Hello, little man.

932
01:01:39,506 --> 01:01:43,434
Boy, I sure heard
a bunch about you.

933
01:01:43,506 --> 01:01:46,604
See, I was a good friend
of your dad's.

934
01:01:46,674 --> 01:01:49,575
We were in that Hanoi
pit of hell together...

935
01:01:49,649 --> 01:01:52,017
over five years.

936
01:01:52,082 --> 01:01:53,936
Hopefully...

937
01:01:54,001 --> 01:01:56,817
you'll never have to
experience this yourself,

938
01:01:56,882 --> 01:02:00,176
but when two men are in a situation
like me and your dad were...

939
01:02:00,242 --> 01:02:02,926
for as long as we were,

940
01:02:02,993 --> 01:02:07,118
you take on certain responsibilities
of the other.

941
01:02:07,186 --> 01:02:09,039
If it'd been me who'd--

942
01:02:10,321 --> 01:02:12,175
not made it,

943
01:02:12,240 --> 01:02:16,332
Major Coolidge'd be talking right now
to my son Jim.

944
01:02:16,400 --> 01:02:19,915
But the way it turned out,
I'm talking to you.

945
01:02:21,264 --> 01:02:23,119
Butch...

946
01:02:24,593 --> 01:02:26,448
I got something for ya.

947
01:02:32,689 --> 01:02:34,662
This watch I got here...

948
01:02:34,736 --> 01:02:39,341
was first purchased
by your great-grandfather
during the first World War.

949
01:02:39,407 --> 01:02:43,881
It was bought in a little general store
in Knoxville, Tennessee.

950
01:02:43,952 --> 01:02:47,367
Made by the first company
to ever make wristwatches.

951
01:02:47,439 --> 01:02:50,254
Up 'til then, people just
carried pocket watches.

952
01:02:50,320 --> 01:02:53,352
It was bought
by Private Doughboy Erine Coolidge...

953
01:02:53,423 --> 01:02:56,239
on the day he set sail for Paris.

954
01:02:56,304 --> 01:02:58,638
This was your
great-grandfather's war watch,

955
01:02:58,703 --> 01:03:01,931
and he wore it every day
he was in that war, and...

956
01:03:01,999 --> 01:03:05,415
when he'd done his duty,
he went home to your great-grandmother,

957
01:03:05,488 --> 01:03:09,743
took the watch off,
put it in an old coffee can,
and in that can it stayed...

958
01:03:09,808 --> 01:03:14,063
until your granddad, Dane Coolidge,
was called upon by his country...

959
01:03:14,128 --> 01:03:17,705
to go overseas and fight
the Germans once again.

960
01:03:17,775 --> 01:03:21,092
This time they called it
World War ll.

961
01:03:21,167 --> 01:03:25,955
Your great-grandfather gave this watch
to your granddad for good luck.

962
01:03:26,030 --> 01:03:28,901
Unfortunately, Dane's luck
wasn't as good as his old man's.

963
01:03:28,975 --> 01:03:31,789
Dane was a Marine,
and he was killed...

964
01:03:31,854 --> 01:03:35,716
along with all the other Marines
at the battle of Wake lsland.

965
01:03:35,790 --> 01:03:38,605
Your granddad was facing death.

966
01:03:38,669 --> 01:03:40,524
He knew it.

967
01:03:40,589 --> 01:03:44,365
None of those boys ever
had any illusions about
leaving that island alive,

968
01:03:44,430 --> 01:03:47,495
so three days before the Japanese
took the island,

969
01:03:47,565 --> 01:03:52,585
your granddad asked
a gunner on an Air Force transport,
name of Winocki--

970
01:03:52,655 --> 01:03:55,469
a man he'd never met before
in his life--

971
01:03:55,534 --> 01:03:58,382
to deliver to his infant son,

972
01:03:58,447 --> 01:04:02,853
who he'd never seen in the flesh,
his gold watch.

973
01:04:02,925 --> 01:04:07,083
Three days later, your granddad
was dead, but Winocki kept his word.

974
01:04:07,150 --> 01:04:11,242
After the war was over,
he paid a visit to your grandmother,

975
01:04:11,310 --> 01:04:15,367
delivering to your infant father
his dad's gold watch.

976
01:04:15,438 --> 01:04:17,292
This watch.

977
01:04:22,926 --> 01:04:28,140
This watch was on your daddy's wrist
when he was shot down over Hanoi.

978
01:04:28,205 --> 01:04:31,500
He was captured,
put in a Vietnamese prison camp.

979
01:04:31,565 --> 01:04:35,461
He knew if the gooks
ever saw the watch,

980
01:04:35,533 --> 01:04:38,914
it'd be confiscated,
taken away.

981
01:04:38,989 --> 01:04:42,534
The way your dad looked at it,
this watch was your birthright.

982
01:04:42,604 --> 01:04:46,379
He'd be damned if any slope's
gonna put their greasy, yellow
hands on his boy's birthright,

983
01:04:46,444 --> 01:04:50,219
so he hid it in one place he knew
he could hide something-- his ass.

984
01:04:50,284 --> 01:04:53,579
Five long years
he wore this watch up his ass.

985
01:04:53,645 --> 01:04:57,670
Then he died of dysentery--
He give me the watch.

986
01:04:57,739 --> 01:05:01,449
I hid this uncomfortable
hunk of metal up my ass two years.

987
01:05:01,516 --> 01:05:03,370
Then...

988
01:05:03,436 --> 01:05:07,331
after seven years,
I was sent home to my family and...

989
01:05:07,404 --> 01:05:09,258
now...

990
01:05:11,596 --> 01:05:14,410
Iittle man,
I give the watch to you.

991
01:05:16,588 --> 01:05:18,442
- [ Bell Rings ]
- [ Gasps ]

992
01:05:18,507 --> 01:05:21,322
[ Crowd Cheering ]

993
01:05:21,387 --> 01:05:24,202
[ Grunting ]

994
01:05:27,691 --> 01:05:30,507
[ Cheering Continues ]

995
01:05:36,331 --> 01:05:38,186
It's time, Butch.

996
01:05:39,755 --> 01:05:42,569
[ Exhaling ]

997
01:05:45,611 --> 01:05:48,425
[ Ring Announcer ]
ln the heavyweight division,

998
01:05:48,491 --> 01:05:51,523
- in the right corner
wearing the blue trunks,
- [ Grunts ]

999
01:05:51,594 --> 01:05:54,725
weighing 210 pounds,

1000
01:05:54,794 --> 01:05:57,794
Floyd Ray Wilson !

1001
01:05:57,866 --> 01:06:00,680
- [ Crowd Cheering, Yelling ]
- [ Bell Rings ]

1002
01:06:00,746 --> 01:06:02,601
[ Announcer ]
It's official. It's official.

1003
01:06:02,667 --> 01:06:05,480
- Wilson is dead !
- [ Announcer
that had to be the bloodiest,

1004
01:06:05,546 --> 01:06:07,880
hands down, the most brutal fight
this city's ever seen.

1005
01:06:07,947 --> 01:06:11,394
Coolidge was out of there
faster than I've ever seen
a victorious boxer leave the ring.

1006
01:06:11,466 --> 01:06:14,280
- Do you think he knew Wilson was dead ?
- My guess would be yes.

1007
01:06:14,346 --> 01:06:17,641
I could see the frenzy in his
eyes give way to the realization
of what he was doing.

1008
01:06:17,706 --> 01:06:21,001
- I think any man would've
left the ring that fast.
- Do you feel this tragedy...

1009
01:06:21,065 --> 01:06:22,920
is gonna affect
the world of boxing ?

1010
01:06:22,986 --> 01:06:26,761
A tragedy like this can't help
but shake the world of boxing
to its very foundations.

1011
01:06:26,825 --> 01:06:30,599
It's of paramount importance,
during the sad weeks ahead,
the eyes of the W.B.A. remain--

1012
01:06:30,666 --> 01:06:33,000
[ Crowd Cheering,
Yelling Continues ]

1013
01:06:34,634 --> 01:06:36,608
- [ Engine Starts ]
- [ Tires Screeching ]

1014
01:06:36,681 --> 01:06:39,496
[ Horn Honking ]

1015
01:07:04,008 --> 01:07:06,244
[ Man ]
Man, you know I didn't--

1016
01:07:06,312 --> 01:07:09,127
- Marsellus.
- No, it wasn't. I didn't do it.

1017
01:07:09,192 --> 01:07:11,048
I didn't do it.

1018
01:07:11,113 --> 01:07:13,502
- How you doing ?
- Great.

1019
01:07:13,577 --> 01:07:15,911
I never thanked you
for dinner.

1020
01:07:17,736 --> 01:07:19,592
- What you got ?
- He booked.

1021
01:07:19,657 --> 01:07:22,623
- His trainer ?
- Says he don't know nothin'.
I believe him.

1022
01:07:22,695 --> 01:07:25,991
- I think Butch surprised
his ass same as us.
- No, we don't wanna "think."

1023
01:07:26,056 --> 01:07:29,503
We wanna know. Take him to
the kennel, sic the dogs on his ass.

1024
01:07:29,575 --> 01:07:32,871
We'll find out for goddamn sure
what he knows and what he don't.

1025
01:07:32,936 --> 01:07:34,791
Butch's search--
How do you want it done ?

1026
01:07:34,855 --> 01:07:37,670
I'm prepared to scour the Earth
for that motherfucker.

1027
01:07:37,735 --> 01:07:41,032
If Butch goes to lndochina, I want
a nigger hiding in a bowl of rice...

1028
01:07:41,096 --> 01:07:43,135
ready to pop a cap in his ass.

1029
01:07:43,207 --> 01:07:45,257
I will take care of it.

1030
01:07:54,599 --> 01:07:56,869
Mister.

1031
01:07:59,656 --> 01:08:02,045
- Hey, mister.
- What ?

1032
01:08:02,119 --> 01:08:06,725
You were in that fight,
the fight on the radio.

1033
01:08:06,793 --> 01:08:10,087
- You're the fighter ?
- Whatever gave you that idea ?

1034
01:08:10,150 --> 01:08:12,801
No, come on.

1035
01:08:12,871 --> 01:08:14,726
You're him.

1036
01:08:14,791 --> 01:08:17,125
I know you're him.

1037
01:08:18,790 --> 01:08:20,614
Tell me you're him.

1038
01:08:20,680 --> 01:08:22,534
I'm him.

1039
01:08:23,590 --> 01:08:25,925
You killed the other boxing man.

1040
01:08:29,415 --> 01:08:31,422
He's dead ?

1041
01:08:31,495 --> 01:08:33,829
The radio said he was dead.

1042
01:08:36,486 --> 01:08:38,624
Sorry about that, Floyd.

1043
01:08:39,879 --> 01:08:42,267
What does it feel like ?

1044
01:08:42,342 --> 01:08:44,197
What does what feel like ?

1045
01:08:44,263 --> 01:08:46,117
Killing a man.

1046
01:08:47,815 --> 01:08:51,709
Beating another man to death
with your bare hands.

1047
01:08:51,782 --> 01:08:53,636
What are you, a weirdo ?

1048
01:08:53,702 --> 01:08:55,557
No.

1049
01:08:55,621 --> 01:08:58,916
It is a subject
I have much interest in.

1050
01:09:00,422 --> 01:09:04,196
You are the first person
I have ever met who has killed somebody.

1051
01:09:06,599 --> 01:09:08,932
So ?

1052
01:09:08,998 --> 01:09:12,130
- What does it feel like to kill a man ?
- [ Sniffs ]

1053
01:09:13,190 --> 01:09:15,044
I'll tell you what.

1054
01:09:15,110 --> 01:09:18,884
Give me one of them cigarettes
you got up there, and I'll
tell you all about it.

1055
01:09:35,877 --> 01:09:38,975
So, Esmarelda...

1056
01:09:40,229 --> 01:09:43,492
Villa Lobos--
Is that Mexican ?

1057
01:09:43,558 --> 01:09:46,656
The name is Spanish,
but I am Colombian.

1058
01:09:46,725 --> 01:09:49,889
- That's some handle
you got there, honey.
- Thank you.

1059
01:09:49,957 --> 01:09:51,812
And what is your name ?

1060
01:09:51,876 --> 01:09:53,502
Butch.

1061
01:09:53,573 --> 01:09:55,940
Butch.

1062
01:09:56,005 --> 01:10:00,576
- What does it mean ?
- I'm an American, honey.
Our names don't mean shit.

1063
01:10:00,645 --> 01:10:03,197
So, moving right along,

1064
01:10:03,268 --> 01:10:05,124
Esmarelda,

1065
01:10:05,190 --> 01:10:07,359
what is it you want to know ?

1066
01:10:07,427 --> 01:10:12,098
- I want to know what it
feels like to kill a man.
- I couldn't tell ya.

1067
01:10:17,765 --> 01:10:22,020
Didn't know he was dead
'til you told me he was dead.

1068
01:10:22,084 --> 01:10:26,492
Now that I know he's dead,
you wanna know how I feel about it ?

1069
01:10:30,084 --> 01:10:33,379
I don't feel
the least bit bad about it.

1070
01:10:43,907 --> 01:10:46,242
What the fuck'd I tell ya ?
Huh ?

1071
01:10:46,308 --> 01:10:50,082
As soon as the word got out
the fix was in, man, the odds
went through the roof.

1072
01:10:50,148 --> 01:10:52,253
I know. I know.
Unbelievable.

1073
01:10:52,323 --> 01:10:55,618
Hey, fuck him, Scotty. If he was
a better boxer, he'd still be alive.

1074
01:10:55,682 --> 01:10:57,537
If he never
laced up his gloves,

1075
01:10:57,603 --> 01:10:59,936
which he never shoulda done in the first
fuckin' place, he'd still be alive.

1076
01:11:00,002 --> 01:11:01,858
[ Hawks, Spits ]

1077
01:11:01,924 --> 01:11:05,371
Yeah, well, who gives a fuck ?
It's over now.

1078
01:11:05,443 --> 01:11:08,257
Yeah, well, enough about the poor,
unfortunate Mr. Floyd.

1079
01:11:08,322 --> 01:11:11,868
Let's talk about the rich
and prosperous Mr. Butch.

1080
01:11:11,938 --> 01:11:14,753
How many bookies did you
lay it around on ?

1081
01:11:14,817 --> 01:11:17,151
All eight ?
How long to collect ?

1082
01:11:18,721 --> 01:11:21,537
So you'll have it all
by tomorrow night ? No, I understand.

1083
01:11:21,602 --> 01:11:24,635
A few stragglers aside.
Oh, fuck, Scotty, that is good news.

1084
01:11:24,707 --> 01:11:26,845
That is great news, man.

1085
01:11:26,914 --> 01:11:30,940
Yeah. Mm-hmm. No, me and Fabienne
are gonna leave in the morning.

1086
01:11:31,010 --> 01:11:34,140
It'll probably take us
a couple days to get down to Knoxville.

1087
01:11:34,209 --> 01:11:36,064
Okay, my brother.

1088
01:11:36,131 --> 01:11:38,017
[ Laughing ]
You're right.

1089
01:11:38,081 --> 01:11:40,317
You're goddamn right.

1090
01:11:40,386 --> 01:11:43,734
All right, Scotty, next time I see you,
it'll be on Tennessee time.

1091
01:11:43,810 --> 01:11:46,046
Cool, brother.

1092
01:12:00,578 --> 01:12:02,912
$45.60.

1093
01:12:06,337 --> 01:12:08,192
And, uh,

1094
01:12:08,257 --> 01:12:11,421
here's a little something
for the effort.

1095
01:12:11,489 --> 01:12:15,263
Now, if anybody asks you who your fare
was tonight, what are you gonna say ?

1096
01:12:15,329 --> 01:12:17,184
The truth.

1097
01:12:17,249 --> 01:12:20,598
Three well-dressed,
slightly toasted Mexicans.

1098
01:12:22,432 --> 01:12:24,734
Bonsoir,
Esmarelda Villa Lobos.

1099
01:12:24,801 --> 01:12:27,221
Buenas Noches, Butch.

1100
01:12:37,887 --> 01:12:39,742
Whew.

1101
01:12:41,056 --> 01:12:42,966
Keep the light off.

1102
01:12:43,040 --> 01:12:45,853
- Is that better, Sugar Pop ?
- Oui.

1103
01:12:45,919 --> 01:12:48,733
- [ Siren Wailing ln Distance ]
- [ Dog Barking ]

1104
01:12:50,143 --> 01:12:51,999
Hard day at the office ?

1105
01:12:52,064 --> 01:12:53,918
Pretty hard.

1106
01:12:53,984 --> 01:12:56,123
Got in a fight.

1107
01:12:56,192 --> 01:12:58,264
Poor baby.

1108
01:12:58,336 --> 01:13:00,791
Can you make spoons ?

1109
01:13:00,863 --> 01:13:03,678
You know what ?
I was thinkin' about takin' a shower.

1110
01:13:03,743 --> 01:13:07,519
- I'm stinkin' like a dog over here.
- I like the way you stink.

1111
01:13:07,584 --> 01:13:09,917
Let me take this jacket off.

1112
01:13:11,998 --> 01:13:15,381
- I was looking at myself in the mirror.
- Uh-huh.

1113
01:13:15,455 --> 01:13:17,310
I wish I had a pot.

1114
01:13:19,007 --> 01:13:22,781
You were looking
at yourself in the mirror,
and you wish you had some pot ?

1115
01:13:22,846 --> 01:13:25,662
A pot. [ Giggles ]
A pot belly.

1116
01:13:25,727 --> 01:13:27,800
Pot bellies are sexy.

1117
01:13:27,871 --> 01:13:30,075
Well, you should be happy,
[ Grunts ]

1118
01:13:30,143 --> 01:13:31,997
'cause you have one.

1119
01:13:32,063 --> 01:13:35,379
Shut up, fatso.
I don't have a pot.

1120
01:13:35,454 --> 01:13:39,164
I have a bit of a tummy,
like Madonna when she did "Lucky Star."

1121
01:13:39,231 --> 01:13:41,085
It's not the same thing.

1122
