- Better tell him to shut up.
He's gettin' on my nerves.
- Fuck. [ Muttering ]

1591
01:48:24,096 --> 01:48:27,162
Marvin. Marvin !
I'd knock that shit off if I was you.

1592
01:48:27,231 --> 01:48:31,224
- [ Door Slams ]
- Die, you motherfuckers ! Die !

1593
01:48:31,296 --> 01:48:33,401
[ Hammer Clicking ]

1594
01:48:58,239 --> 01:49:01,533
Why the fuck didn't you tell us
somebody was in the bathroom ?

1595
01:49:01,598 --> 01:49:04,348
Slip your mind ? Did you forget
that someone was in there...

1596
01:49:04,414 --> 01:49:06,269
with a goddamn hand cannon ?

1597
01:49:06,333 --> 01:49:10,109
You see the size of that gun he fired
at us ? It was bigger than him.

1598
01:49:14,686 --> 01:49:17,273
We should be fuckin' dead, man.

1599
01:49:17,343 --> 01:49:19,196
I know.
We was lucky.

1600
01:49:19,261 --> 01:49:22,262
No, no, no, no.
That shit wasn't luck.

1601
01:49:22,335 --> 01:49:26,360
- Yeah, maybe.
- This was divine intervention.

1602
01:49:26,430 --> 01:49:28,284
You know what
divine intervention is ?

1603
01:49:33,917 --> 01:49:35,772
I think so.

1604
01:49:35,837 --> 01:49:39,133
That means that God came down
from Heaven and stopped the bullets.

1605
01:49:39,198 --> 01:49:41,533
That's right.
That's exactly what it means.

1606
01:49:41,598 --> 01:49:44,444
God came down from Heaven
and stopped these motherfuckin' bullets.

1607
01:49:45,629 --> 01:49:47,538
I think it's time for us
to leave, Jules.

1608
01:49:47,613 --> 01:49:49,948
Don't do that.
Don't fuckin' blow this shit off !

1609
01:49:50,014 --> 01:49:53,788
- What just happened here
was a fuckin' miracle !
- Chill. This shit happens.

1610
01:49:53,854 --> 01:49:56,504
Wrong ! Wrong.
This shit doesn't "just happen."

1611
01:49:56,573 --> 01:49:59,868
Do you want to continue
this theological discussion in a car...

1612
01:49:59,932 --> 01:50:02,267
or in a jailhouse
with the cops ?

1613
01:50:02,333 --> 01:50:04,853
We should be fuckin' dead,
my friend !

1614
01:50:04,925 --> 01:50:08,984
What happened here was a miracle, and I
want you to fucking acknowledge it !

1615
01:50:09,053 --> 01:50:13,559
All right, it was a miracle.
Can we go now ?

1616
01:50:20,285 --> 01:50:23,513
Let's go, nigger !
Come on ! Shit.

1617
01:50:25,316 --> 01:50:27,041
[ Vincent ]
You ever seen that show Cops ?

1618
01:50:27,108 --> 01:50:29,922
I was watching it one time,
and there was this cop on,

1619
01:50:29,988 --> 01:50:33,762
and he was talkin' about this
gunfight he had in the hallway
with this guy, right ?

1620
01:50:33,827 --> 01:50:37,145
He just unloaded on this guy and nothin'
happened. He didn't hit nothin'.

1621
01:50:37,221 --> 01:50:40,034
Okay ? It was just
him and this guy.

1622
01:50:40,100 --> 01:50:43,296
I mean, you know, it's,
it's freaky, but it happens.

1623
01:50:43,363 --> 01:50:48,097
You wanna play blind man,
go walk with the shepherd,
but me, my eyes are wide fuckin' open.

1624
01:50:48,163 --> 01:50:50,977
- What the fuck does that mean ?
- It means that's it for me.

1625
01:50:51,043 --> 01:50:53,629
From here on in, you can
consider my ass retired.

1626
01:50:53,700 --> 01:50:55,773
- Jesus Christ. Goddamn it.
- Don't blaspheme.

1627
01:50:55,844 --> 01:50:58,777
- I said, don't do that !
- Hey, why are you fuckin'
freakin' out on us ?

1628
01:50:58,851 --> 01:51:01,786
Look, I'm tellin' Marsellus today--
I'm through.

1629
01:51:01,859 --> 01:51:04,674
- Why don't you tell him
at the same time why ?
- Don't worry, I will.

1630
01:51:04,739 --> 01:51:08,568
- And I bet you $10,000
he laughs his ass off.
- I don't give a damn if he does.

1631
01:51:08,644 --> 01:51:11,610
[ Sighs ]
Marvin, what do you make of all this ?

1632
01:51:11,683 --> 01:51:14,018
Man, I don't even
have an opinion.

1633
01:51:14,083 --> 01:51:18,140
You gotta have an opinion. You think
God came down from Heaven and stopped--

1634
01:51:18,210 --> 01:51:20,120
- [ Gunshot ]
- What the fuck's happenin' ?

1635
01:51:20,194 --> 01:51:22,049
- Aw, shit, man !
- Aw, man !

1636
01:51:22,114 --> 01:51:24,928
- Oh, man, I shot Marvin in the face.
- Why the fuck'd you do that ?

1637
01:51:24,993 --> 01:51:26,849
I didn't mean it.
It was an accident.

1638
01:51:26,915 --> 01:51:29,729
- Man, I seen some crazy-ass
shit in my time, but this--
- Chill out, man !

1639
01:51:29,794 --> 01:51:32,609
It was an accident. We probably
went over a bump or somethin'.

1640
01:51:32,674 --> 01:51:34,530
The car ain't hit
no motherfuckin' bump.

1641
01:51:34,594 --> 01:51:37,789
I didn't mean to shoot
the son of a bitch. The gun went off.

1642
01:51:37,858 --> 01:51:41,154
Look at this fuckin' mess ! We're on
a city street in broad daylight here !

1643
01:51:41,218 --> 01:51:44,033
- I don't believe it !
- Well, believe it now, motherfucker !

1644
01:51:44,098 --> 01:51:47,414
We gotta get this car off
the road. Cops notice shit
like a car drenched in blood.

1645
01:51:47,490 --> 01:51:50,304
- Just take it to
a friendly place, that's all !
- This is the Valley, Vincent.

1646
01:51:50,370 --> 01:51:52,704
Marsellus ain't got
no friendly places in the Valley.

1647
01:51:52,770 --> 01:51:55,584
- Well, Jules, this ain't
my fuckin' town, man !
- Shit !

1648
01:51:55,650 --> 01:51:58,465
- What you doing ?
- I'm calling my partner in Toluca Lake.

1649
01:51:58,531 --> 01:52:01,911
-Where's Toluca Lake ?
-Over the hill here, by Burbank Studios.

1650
01:52:01,984 --> 01:52:04,800
If Jimmie's ass ain't home,
I don't know what the fuck we gonna do,

1651
01:52:04,865 --> 01:52:07,680
'cause I ain't got
no other partners in 818.

1652
01:52:07,744 --> 01:52:10,559
Jimmie, how you doin', man ?
It's Jules. Just listen up, man.

1653
01:52:10,624 --> 01:52:14,399
Me and my homeboy are in a car, and we
gotta get it off the road, pronto.

1654
01:52:14,465 --> 01:52:16,569
I need to use your garage
for a couple hours.

1655
01:52:18,016 --> 01:52:20,831
We gotta be real fuckin' delicate
with this Jimmie situation.

1656
01:52:20,896 --> 01:52:24,377
He's one remark away
from kickin' our asses out the door.

1657
01:52:24,449 --> 01:52:27,264
- If he does, what do we do ?
- We ain't leavin'
'til we make a couple calls,

1658
01:52:27,329 --> 01:52:30,145
but I don't want it to reach
that pitch-- Jimmie's a friend.

1659
01:52:30,210 --> 01:52:33,023
You don't come into your friend's house
and start tellin' him what's what.

1660
01:52:33,089 --> 01:52:34,944
Just tell him
not to be abusive.

1661
01:52:35,009 --> 01:52:36,864
He kinda freaked out back there
when he saw Marvin.

1662
01:52:36,929 --> 01:52:39,962
Put yourself in his position--
It's 8:00 in the morning,
he just woke up.

1663
01:52:40,032 --> 01:52:41,887
He wasn't expectin' this shit.

1664
01:52:41,952 --> 01:52:44,766
We gotta remember here
who's doin' who a favor.

1665
01:52:44,831 --> 01:52:48,606
If that favor means I gotta
take shit, he can stick that
favor straight up his ass.

1666
01:52:48,672 --> 01:52:52,447
- Fuck, nigger, what the fuck'd
you just do to his towel, man ?
- I was dryin' my hands !

1667
01:52:52,512 --> 01:52:55,327
- You're supposed to wash 'em first !
- You watched me wash 'em.

1668
01:52:55,391 --> 01:52:58,807
- I watched you get 'em wet.
- I was washin' 'em.
This shit's hard to get off.

1669
01:52:58,880 --> 01:53:00,734
Maybe if he'd had Lava
I coulda done a better job.

1670
01:53:00,799 --> 01:53:02,655
I used the same
fuckin' soap you did,

1671
01:53:02,720 --> 01:53:05,535
and when I finished, the towel
didn't look like no goddamn maxi-pad !

1672
01:53:05,599 --> 01:53:08,414
What if he was to come in here
and see his towel like this ?

1673
01:53:08,479 --> 01:53:12,408
It's shit like this that's gonna bring
this situation to a head, man !

1674
01:53:12,480 --> 01:53:15,774
Look, I ain't threatenin' you
or nothin', all right ?

1675
01:53:15,840 --> 01:53:20,117
You know I respect you and all.
But just don't put me
in this position, all right ?

1676
01:53:20,191 --> 01:53:22,776
All right.
Fine. Fine.

1677
01:53:22,847 --> 01:53:25,663
Ask me nice like that,
no problem.

1678
01:53:25,728 --> 01:53:28,543
Just go handle your friend.
Go ahead. I don't care.

1679
01:53:30,207 --> 01:53:32,956
Mmm ! Goddamn, Jimmie !

1680
01:53:33,023 --> 01:53:35,030
This some serious
gourmet shit.

1681
01:53:35,102 --> 01:53:36,958
Me and Vincent
would've been satisfied...

1682
01:53:37,023 --> 01:53:38,910
with some freeze-dried
Taster's Choice.

1683
01:53:38,975 --> 01:53:40,830
Right ?
[ Chuckles ]

1684
01:53:40,894 --> 01:53:43,709
And he springs this
serious gourmet shit on us.

1685
01:53:43,774 --> 01:53:45,749
- What flavor is this ?
- Knock it off, Julie.

1686
01:53:45,822 --> 01:53:49,685
- What ?
- I don't need you to tell me
how fuckin' good my coffee is.

1687
01:53:49,759 --> 01:53:52,146
I'm the one who buys it.
I know how good it is.

1688
01:53:52,222 --> 01:53:54,078
When Bonnie goes shopping,
she buys shit.

1689
01:53:54,143 --> 01:53:57,622
I buy the gourmet expensive stuff 'cause
when I drink it, I wanna taste it.

1690
01:53:57,693 --> 01:54:01,468
But you know what's on
my mind right now ? It ain't
the coffee in my kitchen.

1691
01:54:01,534 --> 01:54:03,606
It's the dead nigger
in my garage.

1692
01:54:03,678 --> 01:54:06,974
- Jimmie, don't even worry--
- Don't tell me about anything.
I wanna ask you a question.

1693
01:54:07,038 --> 01:54:08,892
When you came pulling in here,

1694
01:54:08,958 --> 01:54:12,023
did you notice the sign
on the front of my house that said,
"Dead Nigger Storage" ?

1695
01:54:12,093 --> 01:54:15,389
- You know I ain't seen no--
- Did you notice the sign on
the front of my house...

1696
01:54:15,455 --> 01:54:17,309
that said,
"Dead Nigger Storage" ?

1697
01:54:17,374 --> 01:54:19,992
No. I didn't.

1698
01:54:20,062 --> 01:54:22,876
- You know why you didn't
see that sign ?
- [ Sighs ] Why ?

1699
01:54:22,942 --> 01:54:27,284
'Cause it ain't there,
'cause storing dead niggers
ain't my fuckin' business, that's why !

1700
01:54:27,357 --> 01:54:30,172
- We're not gonna store
the motherfucker--
- Don't you fuckin' realize...

1701
01:54:30,237 --> 01:54:34,492
that if Bonnie comes home and
finds a dead body in her house,
I'm gonna get divorced ?

1702
01:54:34,557 --> 01:54:37,655
No marriage counselor.
No trial separation.
I'm gonna get fuckin' divorced.

1703
01:54:37,724 --> 01:54:40,955
Okay ? And I don't wanna
get fuckin' divorced !

1704
01:54:41,022 --> 01:54:45,810
Man, you know, fuck, I wanna help you,
but I don't wanna lose my wife doin' it.

1705
01:54:45,884 --> 01:54:47,891
Jimmie, Jimmie,
she ain't gonna leave you.

1706
01:54:47,964 --> 01:54:51,739
Don't fuckin' "Jimmie" me, Jules !
Okay ? Don't fuckin' "Jimmie" me.

1707
01:54:51,804 --> 01:54:55,602
There's nothin' you're gonna
say that's gonna make me forget
I love my wife. Is there ?

1708
01:54:58,620 --> 01:55:03,093
Now, look, you know, she comes home
from work in about an hour and a half.

1709
01:55:03,164 --> 01:55:06,098
The graveyard shift
at the hospital.

1710
01:55:06,171 --> 01:55:09,107
You gotta make some phone calls ?
You gotta call some people ?

1711
01:55:09,179 --> 01:55:12,954
Well, then, do it, and then get the fuck
out of my house before she gets here.

1712
01:55:13,020 --> 01:55:15,834
That's Kool and the Gang.
We don't wanna fuck your shit up.

1713
01:55:15,900 --> 01:55:18,747
All I wanna do is call my people
and get 'em to bring us in.

1714
01:55:18,811 --> 01:55:21,627
You're fucking my shit up
right now !

1715
01:55:21,692 --> 01:55:24,659
You're gonna fuck my shit up
big time if Bonnie comes home.

1716
01:55:24,731 --> 01:55:28,081
Do me that favor, all right ?
The phone is in my bedroom.
I suggest you get going.

1717
01:55:28,156 --> 01:55:30,971
Well, say she comes home.

1718
01:55:31,036 --> 01:55:33,369
What do you think she'll do ?

1719
01:55:34,812 --> 01:55:37,145
Oh, no fuckin' shit she'll freak.

1720
01:55:37,212 --> 01:55:39,316
That ain't no kinda answer.

1721
01:55:39,386 --> 01:55:42,322
I mean, you know, I don't.
How much ? A lot or a little ?

1722
01:55:42,395 --> 01:55:45,145
You got to appreciate
what an explosive element...

1723
01:55:45,211 --> 01:55:47,066
this Bonnie situation is.

1724
01:55:47,132 --> 01:55:50,906
She comes home from a hard day's work,
finds a bunch of gangsters
in her kitchen...

1725
01:55:50,970 --> 01:55:52,825
doing a bunch of gangster shit,

1726
01:55:52,890 --> 01:55:55,825
there ain't no tellin'
what she's liable to do.

1727
01:55:55,899 --> 01:55:57,841
[ All Gasping ]

1728
01:55:57,914 --> 01:55:59,770
Yeah, I grasp that, Jules.

1729
01:55:59,836 --> 01:56:02,323
All I'm doing is
contemplating the ifs.

1730
01:56:02,395 --> 01:56:05,210
I don't wanna hear about
no motherfuckin' ifs !

1731
01:56:05,275 --> 01:56:09,049
All I want to hear from your ass
is, "You ain't got no problem,
Jules. I'm on the motherfucker.

1732
01:56:09,114 --> 01:56:13,108
Chill them niggers out
and wait for the cavalry,
which should be coming directly."

1733
01:56:13,179 --> 01:56:16,211
You ain't got no problem, Jules.

1734
01:56:16,281 --> 01:56:18,321
I'm on the motherfucker.

1735
01:56:18,393 --> 01:56:23,248
Chill them niggers out and wait for
the Wolf, who should be coming directly.

1736
01:56:23,322 --> 01:56:25,657
You sendin' the Wolf ?

1737
01:56:25,721 --> 01:56:27,827
Oh, you feel better,
motherfucker ?

1738
01:56:27,897 --> 01:56:30,069
Shit, yeah, negro !

1739
01:56:30,138 --> 01:56:33,138
That's all you had to say !

1740
01:56:33,209 --> 01:56:36,276
-  [ Piano ]
- [ Man ] She the hysterical type ?

1741
01:56:36,346 --> 01:56:39,159
- When is she due ?
- [ Partygoers Chattering ]

1742
01:56:39,225 --> 01:56:41,233
Mm-hmm.

1743
01:56:41,305 --> 01:56:43,160
Give me
the principals' names again.

1744
01:56:43,226 --> 01:56:45,081
[ Man ]
Place your bets.

1745
01:56:46,104 --> 01:56:49,619
- Jules. Mm-hmm.
- Cards, please.

1746
01:56:49,690 --> 01:56:51,544
Vincent.

1747
01:56:56,089 --> 01:56:57,944
Jimmie.

1748
01:56:59,128 --> 01:57:01,168
Bonnie. Mm-hmm.

1749
01:57:06,361 --> 01:57:09,330
It's thirty minutes away.
I'll be there in ten.

1750
01:57:10,738 --> 01:57:13,073
[ Tires Screeching ]

1751
01:57:22,034 --> 01:57:23,661
[ Doorbell Rings ]

1752
01:57:25,459 --> 01:57:28,274
You're... Jimmie, right ?
This is your house ?

1753
01:57:28,338 --> 01:57:31,819
- It sure is.
- I'm Winston Wolf. I solve problems.

1754
01:57:31,891 --> 01:57:34,705
- Good. We got one.
- So I heard. May I come in ?

1755
01:57:34,770 --> 01:57:36,626
Uh, yeah. Please do.

1756
01:57:36,691 --> 01:57:40,202
You must be Jules.
Which would make you... Vincent.

1757
01:57:40,273 --> 01:57:42,609
Let's get down
to brass tacks, gentlemen.

1758
01:57:42,674 --> 01:57:45,488
If I was informed correctly, the clock
is ticking. Is that right, Jimmie ?

1759
01:57:45,553 --> 01:57:47,408
Uh, one hundred percent.

1760
01:57:47,474 --> 01:57:51,249
- Your wife Bonnie comes home
at 9:30 in the a.m., correct ?
- Uh-huh.

1761
01:57:51,314 --> 01:57:55,624
I was led to believe if she
comes home and finds us here,
she wouldn't appreciate it much.

1762
01:57:55,697 --> 01:57:59,822
- She wouldn't at that.
- That gives us 40 minutes
to get the fuck outta Dodge,

1763
01:57:59,891 --> 01:58:03,184
which, if you do what I say,
when I say it, should be plenty.

1764
01:58:03,248 --> 01:58:07,406
Now, you got a corpse
in a car, minus a head,
in a garage. Take me to it.

1765
01:58:11,281 --> 01:58:13,136
[ Sighs ]

1766
01:58:14,834 --> 01:58:16,688
- Jimmie.
- Uh-huh.

1767
01:58:16,753 --> 01:58:20,048
Do me a favor, will ya ? Thought I
smelled some coffee back there.

1768
01:58:20,113 --> 01:58:23,408
- Would you make me a cup ?
- Uh, yeah, sure.

1769
01:58:24,816 --> 01:58:27,632
Oh, uh, um,
how do you take it ?

1770
01:58:27,697 --> 01:58:30,152
Lotsa cream, lotsa sugar.

1771
01:58:32,145 --> 01:58:35,439
About the car, is there anything
I need to know ? Does it stall ?

1772
01:58:35,504 --> 01:58:38,800
Does it smoke ? Does it make
a lot of noise ? ls there gas in it ?

1773
01:58:38,864 --> 01:58:42,160
- Aside from how it looks,
the car's cool.
- Positive ?

1774
01:58:42,224 --> 01:58:45,519
Don't get me on the road and I find out
the brake lights don't work.

1775
01:58:45,584 --> 01:58:49,479
- As far as I know,
the motherfucker's tip-top.
- Good enough.

1776
01:58:49,553 --> 01:58:51,494
Let's go back
to the kitchen.

1777
01:58:54,511 --> 01:58:56,845
[ Exhales ]

1778
01:58:56,912 --> 01:58:59,727
- Here you go, Mr. Wolf.
- Thank you, Jimmie.

1779
01:59:04,367 --> 01:59:06,222
Mmm.

1780
01:59:07,247 --> 01:59:09,287
Okay, first thing.
You two.

1781
01:59:09,360 --> 01:59:12,174
Take the body,
stick it in the trunk.

1782
01:59:12,239 --> 01:59:14,857
This looks to be
a pretty domesticated house.

1783
01:59:14,926 --> 01:59:18,701
- That would lead me to believe
you got cleansers and shit.
- Yeah. Under the sink.

1784
01:59:18,766 --> 01:59:22,061
Good. What I need you two fellas to do
is take those cleaning products...

1785
01:59:22,128 --> 01:59:25,989
and clean the inside of the car--
I'm talkin' fast, fast, fast.

1786
01:59:26,063 --> 01:59:29,837
Go in the back seat, scoop up all
those little pieces of brain and skull.

1787
01:59:29,903 --> 01:59:32,717
Get it out of there.
Wipe down the upholstery.

1788
01:59:32,783 --> 01:59:35,597
It don't need to be spick-and-span.
You don't need to eat off it.

1789
01:59:35,663 --> 01:59:39,852
Just give it a good once-over.
What you need to take care of
are the really messy parts.

1790
01:59:39,919 --> 01:59:43,847
The pools of blood that have collected,
you gotta soak that shit up.

1791
01:59:43,918 --> 01:59:46,252
We need to raid
your linen closet.

1792
01:59:46,318 --> 01:59:49,132
I need blankets,
I need comforters, quilts, bedspreads.

1793
01:59:49,199 --> 01:59:52,678
The thicker the better,
the darker the better.
No whites. Can't use 'em.

1794
01:59:52,750 --> 01:59:57,835
We'll need to camouflage the front seat
